# Products setting page

Merchandise **Edit** on `/products` opens a compact popup (`ProductEditPopup`): selling fields, size/drop subset (on-hand lock), size upcharges, photos, Save as template. The Fit List row stays one line. There is no Settings column.

**Photos** for the product sit in a panel to the left of the edit card: thumbnails stacked vertically, large image beneath. **Search** on the Photos panel opens a photo-site popup. Click pictures, then **Select** adds them or **Cancel** closes with no change. **Remove** drops one from the panel. Either change shows **Save** on the edit card; nothing is written until that Save. Cancel on the edit card leaves the stored photos unchanged. The database stores the path on `product_images`. The host is `PRODUCT_IMAGE_ORIGIN`, set per deploy. **Filter** on this page: **Lot #** is a Combo Box of the lot numbers on the list and still accepts a typed lot (`allowAny`, contains). **Model** lists models of the chosen **Item**; a blank Item lists every model, and choosing an item clears a model from another item. The merchandise Fit List shows the same thumbnail at the left of the product name. A product with no photo keeps an empty 64×72 slot so the names line up. Charges and freight have no thumbnail. Inventory shows one thumbnail in each row, in the same column as the grand total and above that number. Hovering it floats a larger copy of the full photo over the size grid; the row does not move. A click opens a view-only photo window: larger thumbnails in a panel on the left, the large image beside them. The size grid stays in the row.

Charges & freight still edit inline on their Fit List.

`/products/[id]` is leftover (alerts). Do not add Fit List Settings links back.

When the user says **products setting page** or product settings, change this popup—not a new route.
